        "content": "<p>We are moving away from the PMF implementation (basic discrete measures such as Poisson, binomial and Bernoulli have been redefined to get rid of PMF) so I think this does not fit mathlib.</p>",
        "id": 613297274,
        "sender_full_name": "Etienne Marion",
        "timestamp": 1785274602
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do you have a pointer to the documentation explaining what the new design is? I'd love to learn more about it.</p>",
        "id": 613301056,
        "sender_full_name": "Hannah Leung",
        "timestamp": 1785276715
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can have a look at how the measures I mentioned are defined now, basically we use sums of Dirac masses (except for binomial which is defined a bit differently). See <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/generic.20shannon.20entropy.20formalization.20mathlib4/near/584361371\">https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/generic.20shannon.20entropy.20formalization.20mathlib4/near/584361371</a> for pointers to some PRs where some discussion the topic happened.</p>",
